    "result_text": "Done. The full build is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`).\n\n## What I changed\n\nThe spec: *on successful create, enqueue a welcome notification \u2014 emit via the logger named `NOTIFY` a line containing the owner id and the memberId.*\n\nI added one small OfficeFloor function step rather than touching the existing `AUDIT`-logger step, keeping one responsibility per class.\n\n**New function** \u2014 `src/main/java/.../rest/function/owner/EnqueueWelcomeNotification.java`:\n```java\npublic class EnqueueWelcomeNotification {\n    private static final Logger notify = LoggerFactory.getLogger(\"NOTIFY\");\n\n    public void service(@Val Owner owner) {\n        notify.info(\"welcome owner id={} memberId={}\", owner.getId(), owner.getMemberId());\n    }\n}\n```\n\n**Wiring** \u2014 in `owners.POST.yml`, inserted an `enqueueWelcome` step between `audit` and `respond`. It reads the saved owner via `@Val` (so `id` and `memberId` are both already populated) and carries `govern: [ transaction ]` to match the surrounding steps.\n\n```yaml\naudit:\n  ...\n  next: enqueueWelcome\n\nenqueueWelcome:\n  class: org.springframework.samples.petclinic.rest.function.owner.EnqueueWelcomeNotification\n  govern: [ transaction ]\n  next: respond\n```\n\nThe new `AcceptanceTest.coreEnqueuesWelcome` passes \u2014 the test captures the `NOTIFY` logger and the emitted line (`welcome owner id=11 memberId=NSW2716E6609E1`) contains both the owner id and the memberId.",
